+phase carries timing_plan_sha256 and timing_result_sha256 for immutable artifacts
+under timing/{states.EVALUATION.cycle}/ (cycle1..3). The Write/Edit hook blocks
+PLANNING without reproduced analysis evidence and COMPLETION without a verified
+paired defense bound matching current oracle source commits. Removing the kind,
+changing frozen bindings outside diagnosis or skipping the bounded cycle is
+rejected. The oracle completion CLI checks the same artifact boundary, including
+retained timing artifacts whose classification was removed by a direct edit.
+
+AWAITING_OBSERVATION/INCONCLUSIVE/ERROR remain in ANALYSIS; do not set its status
+completed or reproduction_confirmed=true. An actual RECURRED monitor event requests
+ANALYSIS resume with a fresh bounded generation, not fix acceptance. Infrastructure,
+normal-control, injection and cleanup failures are separate factual branches.
+Statistics and node ownership remain ChainBench's responsibility. Existing primary/
+independent oracle, candidate-selection and verification gates still apply.
