+---
+name: timing-investigation
+description: "Freeze bounded timing/fault investigations, retain factual ChainBench receipts, and keep unreproduced symptoms in observation rather than accepting a fix."
+type: skill
+---
+
+# Timing evidence before diagnosis or completion
+
+Use this route for nondeterministic/ordering/fault symptoms. Set
+`states.ANALYSIS.investigation_kind` to `timing` (or `observation`) before freezing
+any trial. Keep the primary/independent oracle and fix-selection gates; these
+receipts do not replace them or grant cause acceptance.
+
+1. Read source coordinates and requirements. Freeze the complete public
+   ChainBench input: before/after clean Go binaries and immutable commits,
+   whole DSL, normal controls, designated symptom assertion, environment and
+   external file hashes, deterministic seed/schedules, repetition and time
+   budgets, explicit injection step/target and fresh owned artifact root.
+   Every usable trial contains its own normal-control branch. Comparison uses
+   paired schedules for reproduction before and defense after. Statistical
+   acceptance is the provider's observed bound, never an impossibility claim.
+2. Use `chainbench_experiment` with the real nested input schema, exposed as
+   `mcp__plugin_coding-agent_chainbench__chainbench_experiment`. The bundled
+   `contracts/chainbench-tools.schema.json` captures current tools/list inputs.
+   Compare the actual server contract using `--check-contract` before assuming
+   compatibility. Legacy init/start/test-run recipes describe another surface;
+   do not guess or silently call those names for this timing route.
+3. The bundled runner can execute the same app path through the pinned public
+   CLI. Freeze while current_state is ANALYSIS/EVALUATION respectively and
+   record the emitted plan SHA in that phase BEFORE execution. Analysis permits
+   reproduction/observation; evaluation requires comparison with >=30 planned
+   and minimum-completed samples. Plan and result names are under
+   `timing/{states.EVALUATION.cycle}/`, with cycle1..3. Never overwrite a phase.
+
+```sh
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/timing_investigation.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --phase analysis --freeze proposal.json --chainbench "$CHAINBENCH_BIN" --ticket-id "{ticket_id}"
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/timing_investigation.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --phase analysis --execute
+python3 "${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/timing_investigation.py" --workspace "{workspace_dir}" --phase analysis --check
+```
+
+The state-bound automated route uses the runner CLI. A direct MCP diagnostic
+call does not fabricate that CLI execution receipt; never reuse its artifact
+root for a second run. Keep the direct tool response as separate evidence.
+
+4. The runner writes immutable proposed/prepared pins, controller stdout/stderr,
+   execution command/exit receipt, raw report and projected normal/reproduction/
+   defense/observation branches. It re-runs ChainBench's raw receipt/accounting
+   verifier; it does not duplicate graph or statistics computations. Bind the
+   exact result file SHA to `states.<PHASE>.timing_result_sha256`, then use
+   `--check-state`. Verify remains read-only; execute may allocate and inject
+   only fresh trial-owned nodes as authorized by the frozen input.
+5. Infrastructure error, failed control/injection/cleanup, missing trials and
+   small samples cannot confirm reproduction or repair. `AWAITING_OBSERVATION`
+   stays in ANALYSIS with reproduction_confirmed=false; do not plan a speculative
+   fix or mark analysis completed. A read-only observer freezes an actual existing
+   composition digest and approved RPC predicate, has no node control/keyring,
+   and samples only during its bounded window. `RECURRED` requests diagnosis
+   resume; it does not itself confirm a root cause or pass a defense gate.
+The consumer forwards one interruption to the isolated native controller and
+waits for its independent cleanup. Cancellation never becomes a successful
+defense. It does not use a Python timeout to kill the node controller.
+
+6. A new bounded generation must return to ANALYSIS and increment the existing
+   evaluation cycle by exactly one, retaining old files. Return to a reproduced
+   investigation before PLANNING. An exhausted cycle requires an explicit new
+   scope, not an unlimited silent retry. Unavailable or incompatible servers
+   remain an explicit blocked/unavailable investigation; no invented success.
+7. Evaluation freezes a comparison with the same oracle baseline and current
+   candidate source. Complete only when the provider reports
+   `OBSERVED_RATE_BOUND_MET`, the normal controls/cleanup pass, current source
+   matches the primary/independent oracle evidence, and all existing oracle,
+   candidate-selection and regression gates also pass. The state Write/Edit
+   hook and oracle completion CLI both validate these bindings. They do not
+   sandbox direct shell/manual edits or provide independent human acceptance.
